    body: `CrewCore handles the employee side of P&M's SIMPLE IRA sign-up (added Sep 30 2026): each employee reads the plan info, gets the packet, and records whether they enroll or decline and how much comes out of each paycheck. Ryan collects the signed paper packet and marks it returned. It lives on the Dashboard; there is no separate IRA tab.

## How do I sign up for the SIMPLE IRA in CrewCore
1. Open CrewCore. The "Retirement (IRA)" box is on your Dashboard.
2. Open "What is a SIMPLE IRA?" for the short explanation, and press "Get the packet" to open the IRA packet.
3. Choose "Enroll" or "Decline". For Enroll, enter how much to "Put in" and pick "% of my pay" or "dollars per paycheck". Add the "Effective date" that goes on the paper form.
4. Press "Save my choice".
Choosing does not replace the packet. The box then tells you exactly what to fill in, for example "On the Salary Deferral Election page, check box A (New election for a new account), write 4%, effective date 11/01/2026, then sign and date it. Include the American Funds application pages if you have never had this account." Give the signed pages to Ryan; do not mail anything to American Funds yourself. Until he marks it returned the box says "Ryan does not have your packet yet." To change later, press "Change".

## Which box do I check on the IRA Salary Deferral Election page
CrewCore picks the box from what you had before and what you chose. A: enrolling for the first time (new election for a new account). B: you were enrolled and changed the amount (change deferrals). D: you were enrolled and now decline (suspend deferrals); it asks for the date to stop and warns "Stopping may mean you cannot start again until the next plan year's sign-up period." E: declining when you were never enrolled (no pre-tax salary deferrals at this time); no date is needed. Box C (keep the same, the yearly re-election) is not something CrewCore does. Amounts: a percent from more than 0 up to 100 with at most two decimals, or a dollar amount to the cent, not both.

## How the IRA plan is explained in CrewCore
The plan info says: a SIMPLE IRA is a retirement savings account offered by small businesses; you can put part of each paycheck in, which lowers your taxable income now; P&M matches what you put in, up to the match percent set in Settings (3% by default) of your pay; the money is not taxed until it comes out, usually in retirement; taking money out before age 59 and a half can mean penalties, steeper in your first two years in the plan; to sign up, fill out the Salary Deferral Election page and give it to Ryan, with the American Funds application pages the first time. The match setting only changes these words, not anybody's pay; payroll does the math.

## Who can see IRA choices in CrewCore
Only the employee themselves and CrewCore admins. Nobody else can see whether a coworker enrolled or declined. When someone makes or changes a choice, the time off approvers (Ryan and Megan) get a notification titled "IRA sign-up: a choice to review" (plus ", packet to collect" when paperwork is involved), which deliberately does not name the person or the choice (it is private to each approver, but still shows on screens other people can see); it says to open the IRA sign-up card on the CrewCore Dashboard. Saving the same choice twice does not notify again. CrewCore stores only the choice, the amount, the date and whether the packet came back: no Social Security number, birth date, bank or beneficiary details, which stay on the paper packet.

## The CrewCore IRA sign-up sheet for admins
On the admin Dashboard the "IRA sign-up" card shows how many are enrolled and packets to collect; clicking it scrolls to the "IRA sign-up" sheet. It counts enrolled, declined, not chosen yet, and packets to collect, and lists every current (not terminated) employee with Name, IRA (Enrolled, Declined, Not chosen yet), Contribution, Packet ("to collect" or "returned") and Last changed. Click a row to open that person's IRA box, where an admin can "Set choice"/"Change" on their behalf, press "Mark packet returned" (or "Mark packet not returned"), and see the History. The same box appears on the person's Roster record. "Export CSV" downloads the sheet (Name, Department, IRA, Contribution, Start date, Packet returned, Packet to collect, Last changed). A packet is "to collect" when someone is enrolled and it has not come back, or when they changed their choice after it came back ("Choice changed after the packet came in. A new packet may be needed."); marking it returned clears that. Only admins can mark packets. The packet link and match percent are set in CrewCore Settings under "SIMPLE IRA" (the link must start with http:// or https://).

## Troubleshooting CrewCore IRA messages
"Pick enroll or decline.": choose one. "Say how much to put in from each paycheck.": enrolling needs an amount. "Pick a percent of pay or a dollar amount, not both." "The percent can't be more than 100." "The dollar amount can only go to the cent." "The start date has to be a real date (YYYY-MM-DD)." "You can only see your own IRA choice" or "You can only make your own IRA choice": only admins can see or set someone else's. "Only an admin can mark a packet returned." "Your login isn't linked to an employee record yet. Ask an admin to add it in CrewCore's Roster.": no IRA box appears until the login is linked.`,
